<title>SWEDEN: Swedish consumer prices down 0.2 pct in Dec.</title>
<headline>Swedish consumer prices down 0.2 pct in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish consumer prices fell by 0.2 percent in December which gave average inflation for 1996 of 0.7 percent, Statistics Sweden said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p> SWEDISH CONSUMER PRICES     Dec 96     Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change	 -0.2	 -0.3	   -0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year change	   -0.2	 -0.3	   +2.6</p>
<p> Index (1980=100)		254.9	255.3	 256.0</p>
<p>Note - Economists polled by Reuters had expected consumer prices to fall by 0.3 percent in December.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
